>> Hello. I have some info on that card, but not much. I have discovered=20
>> that this card is detected connected via USB rather than PCI-E (the=20
>> slot is ExpressCard). snd_ctxfi uses PCI interfaces right? Can X-Fi=20
>> support be also added to snd_usb_audio? Or can snd_ctxfi support USB?
>>
>> lsusb -v output on that card is attached (sorry for duplicate mail,=20
>> forgot to attach it first time). I now have this card and willing to=20
>> help to test (or perhaps create) proper driver.
> Additional info. The card is partially recognized - Analog Stereo=20
> Input device is available. But sadly no output.
> Also I tested the card in Virtual Box (WinXP 64 guest) and even=20
> without creative drivers the card is recognized as USB Audio Device=20
> and works fine. So it seems it's usb audio compliant. I hope this is=20
> helpful.
Hmm, it looks like Input working is the result of my addition to=20
alsa-kernel/usb/usbquirks.h
Recording from mic now works (on very low volume though)

/* Creative X-Fi Notebook */
{
     .match_flags =3D USB_DEVICE_ID_MATCH_VENDOR |=20
USB_DEVICE_ID_MATCH_PRODUCT,
     .idVendor =3D 0x041e,
     .idProduct =3D 0x30d2,
     .bInterfaceClass =3D USB_CLASS_AUDIO,
     .driver_info =3D (unsigned long) & (const struct snd_usb_audio_quirk=
) {
         .vendor_name =3D "Creative Labs",
         .product_name =3D "X-Fi Notebook",
         .ifnum =3D QUIRK_NO_INTERFACE
     }
},

I tested some other quirk values but nothing else works at all. As for=20
output - alsamixer actually shows it and allows to change it's volume,=20
but channel number is not available. For example speaker-test says=20
'Error setting hwparams: Invalid argument" and aplay says "Channel=20
number is not available" on any channel number.
alsa-info output is attached.
I ask for any help from experienced alsa developer (snd_usb_audio=20
specifically).

